# Docker does NOT read .gitignore — without this file, `COPY . .` drags the
# host's node_modules into the image and overwrites the one `npm ci` just
# installed. Symlinks in node_modules/.bin get materialised as plain files in
# the process, so `node_modules/.bin/tsc` stops resolving `../lib/tsc.js` and
# the build dies with MODULE_NOT_FOUND.
#
# Keeping the context clean also makes the build reproducible: what gets built
# depends only on package-lock.json, never on whatever happens to be installed
# on the machine running the build.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output — regenerated inside the image.
dist
build
.vite

# Local env and secrets must never enter an image layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Tooling noise that only bloats the context.
.git
.gitignore
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
coverage
.nyc_output

# Tests and editor config are not needed to produce the bundle.
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
.vscode
.idea
